.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt GENCAT 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm gencat
.Nd compile a message catalog
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar catalog
.Ar source ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility compiles one or more message-catalog source files into
.Ar catalog ,
the binary image read by the RavenBSD locale catalog runtime.
The output catalog is replaced, not merged.
.Pp
Supported source lines are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -offset indent
.It Cm $set Ar N
Start or select set
.Ar N .
Set and message ids must be positive.
.It Cm $delset Ar N
Remove set
.Ar N .
.It Cm $transient
Accepted and ignored.
.It Cm $comment Ar text
Accepted and ignored.
.It Ar id Ar string
Define message
.Ar id
in the current set; the string must be quoted.
.El
.Pp
Strings are UTF-8 and support
.Ql \e\e ,
.Ql \e\&" ,
.Ql \en ,
.Ql \et
and
.Ql \er .
Multiple source files share the current set.
The image is limited to 8 MiB.
.Ar catalog
of
.Ar -
writes to standard output.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
0 on success, 1 for a source or output error, 2 for usage.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr iconv 1 ,
.Xr locale 1
.Sh STANDARDS
A documented subset of POSIX
.Nm gencat .
Merging, multi-line messages, adjacent string concatenation, octal/hex escapes, symbolic set
names and
.Cm $codeset
are unsupported.
